> One thing to think about is order: if we do what your PR proposes, we are altering the order in which plugins are run, not just modifying the "weight" of the plugin.

It's the key point I'm concerned about: commented here https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/99582#discussion_r588799737. So let me ask a question: for a given input like:

```go
customPlugins: &Plugins{
	Filter: PluginSet{
		Enabled: []Plugin{
			{Name: "DefaultPlugin2", Weight: 200},
		},
		Disabled: []Plugin{
			{Name: "DefaultPlugin2", Weight: 2},
		},
	},
},
defaultPlugins: &Plugins{
	Filter: PluginSet{
		Enabled: []Plugin{
			{Name: "DefaultPlugin1", Weight: 1},
			{Name: "DefaultPlugin2", Weight: 2},
			{Name: "DefaultPlugin3", Weight: 3},
		},
	},
},
```

What's the expected output?

1. {DefaultPlugin1, 1}, {DefaultPlugin2, 200}, {DefaultPlugin3, 3}, OR
1. {DefaultPlugin1, 1}, {DefaultPlugin3, 3}, {DefaultPlugin2, 200}
